1.3
1.3.1
client -> url service -> database
client -> api gateway -> (url redirection service , url shortening service , analytics service) -> (database+cache)
                                     |> counter                                                  (adding in-memory)=> store count
so, cache => for optimizing short url access
in-memory (store count) => used for analytics

1.3.2
but , in this case api gateway is overkill because we only have two services.
api gateway decides which service the request should go to.

1.3.3
tradeoff between caching and analytics , if use caching , we won't be able to do link analytics , if
we have to do link analytics , then don't do caching.

1.3.4
-> Short URL Generation , Base-62 encoding (A-Z,a-z,0-9)  _ _ _ _ _ _ (62^6) 
   6-7 characters short url length.
-> Short URL will be stored in the database with format :-
            shortUrl : string
            longUrl : string
            uid : string
            created_at : date
            used_count : int

1kb * 1 Billion = 5 TB

1.3.5
How to generate unique short URLs ?
(i)
-> using counter by implementing it useing redis cache (by using key-value pair)
-> downside :- single point of failure 
-> upside :- redis is single threaded so no need to worry about concurrency issues.

(ii)
-> randomly generating strings by using md5 or sha256.
-> collision can occur , but can be solved by using retries.
-> no need to optimize the latency in URL shortening service => < 5 seconds is fine,o/w overkill

-> optimizing url redirection service :- 10K RPS => using vertical scaling , 
                       now-a-days , vertical scaling can handle at most 100 k requests/second
                                                 or read replica sets <= use caching instead of this
                                                    sharding (will be overkill)

-> so, latency is reduced and throughput is improved

(iv)
analytics
=> using in-memory (for storing count for analytics)
=> from url generation service , you can directly update the databse , because this operation does
   not happen many times ,
=> but the same thing can't be done for url redirection service , because it is read-intensive.
   so , that's why using in-memory , and it will periodically flush the data into the database.

